2.1.8.3

- Expanded Bingo with standard and custom games, more patterns and round controls. Refined other Arcade games and their on-screen feedback.
- Improved browser audio and video synchronisation and fixed approved redirects being cancelled.
- Added an update notice in the sidebar. Changed the combat/cutscene playback option to **Stop**, with playback remaining stopped until resumed.

## 2.1.8.2

- Added compact broadcast controls and setup popups for Browser, Retro Games and Local Video.
- Creating a Watch Party from these pages leaves broadcasting off until you choose **Start Broadcast**.
- Added a game/FFXIV control switcher to the mini dock and fixed page controls being hidden behind the playback bar.

## 2.1.8.1

- Improved browser broadcast startup by waiting for playable audio and video before starting.
- Fixed the featured room **Join** button. Emulator controls now release held buttons when FFXIV loses focus.
- Improved stability when restarting broadcasts, closing the browser or replacing images.

## 2.1.8.0

- Fixed browser broadcasts stuttering after dropped audio and increased the viewer’s initial buffering.

## 2.1.7.9

- Improved diagnostics for browser broadcasts that stall or lag.

## 2.1.7.8

- Fixed notification sound previews only playing the first time.

## 2.1.7.7

- Added automatic hardware encoding selection for supported NVIDIA, Intel and AMD systems, with software fallback for supported broadcast sources.
- Opening a supported game file from the library now switches to its console automatically.

## 2.1.7.6

- Added optional notification sounds for friend requests and chat messages.
- Added auto-apply for TV presets and improved TV placement and syncing after travel, duty entry and respawning.
- Reduced the graphics workload of enhanced music visualisers. Clarified when an active broadcast or game needs to end before transferring host.

## 2.1.7.5

- Improved Watch Party handovers so shared video and radio keep playing with their position, subtitles and TV placement.
- Added a TV reset-position shortcut and moved active playback to the Mini Player when entering duties.
- Added clearer friend removal confirmation and improved media startup and cleanup.

## 2.1.7.4

- Updated the XIVAuth sign-in popup and added confirmation before blocking someone.
- Added unread message counts to the Friends page and a **Switch Queue** shortcut.

## 2.1.7.3

- Improved live broadcast startup and subtitle selection. English and Off are easy to find, and the active track has a checkmark.
- Added a shared friend-request and unread-message badge. Chromium downloads when the other startup components are ready.

## 2.1.7.2

- Fixed audio compatibility for local-video broadcasts by using stereo AAC for viewers.

## 2.1.7.1

- Updated first launch to offer XIVAuth or guest access, a username and topic choices.
- Expanded The Arcade and refreshed Watch Party activity layouts, including the React Live banner.
- Improved Continue Watching, live radio resume, volume controls and YouTube loading indicators.

## 2.1.7.0

- Added the target-shooting activity that became **Air Force EX**, with a ready check and shared rounds.
- Fixed a crash that could occur when stopping native playback, including sounds used by Choco RaceBets.

## 2.1.6.9

- Added **Choco RaceBets**, with six racers, a betting countdown, changing race conditions and a results ledger.
- Refined the track, race pacing, payouts and sound effects.

## 2.1.6.8

- Made volume settings consistent across controls and saved the chosen volume between sessions.
- Added a Pictionary results screen and expanded the word list.
- Improved compatibility with other plugins using the same media playback library.

## 2.1.6.7

- Redesigned the Activities page with clearer cards and a consistent grid.
- Added Roulette rules and improved the betting ledger.

## 2.1.6.6

- Fixed shared Pictionary drawing going out of sync between rounds.

## 2.1.6.5

- Added **Quiz** with Quick Play and custom settings.
- Expanded **Roulette** with a setup screen, configurable play, improved feedback and wheel sounds.
- Improved Pictionary scoreboards and long on-screen announcements.

## 2.1.6.4

- Added group chat creation from the Friends list and clearer video request cards.
- Expanded Pictionary’s word list, improved round feedback and reduced unnecessary chat notifications.
- Entering instanced content preserves the Watch Party connection. Retro-game broadcasts can pause after inactivity.

## 2.1.6.3

- Added shared drawing with solo and team modes and expanded Pictionary.
- Added more live reactions and improved TV position-sync controls. Watch Party chat now supports removing your reactions and deleting permitted messages.
- Improved login storage reliability.

## 2.1.6.2

- Redesigned Friends and Watch Party pages with a more compact dashboard.
- Added the **React Live** hotbar and matched in-game reaction icons and colours to chat. Reactions can appear near the sender’s on-screen position.

## 2.1.6.1

- Improved 4K interface scaling and window resizing.
- Refreshed Home and Add Media layouts and improved browsing and subscriptions for YouTube and Internet Archive.
- Added clearer broadcasting controls and Patreon access guidance while keeping solo playback available.

## 2.1.6.0

- Improved TV startup when joining a party, viewer startup for Game Boy Advance broadcasts and the host’s DJ visualiser.
- Choosing ordinary playback keeps you on the media page you’re browsing.

## 2.1.5.9

- Added NES and Game Boy Advance support and improved the retro game library and controls.
- Added an embedded browser with favourites, history, privacy controls and an in-game TV view.
- Added a dedicated Mini Player and improved how current media carries over when starting a Watch Party.
- Added encrypted local login storage and clearer sign-in recovery.
